✅ Core Features of Java


1. Object-Oriented
Everything in Java is based on objects and classes.

Supports key OOP principles: Inheritance, Polymorphism, Encapsulation, and Abstraction.

2. Platform Independent
"Write once, run anywhere" — Java code is compiled into bytecode, which runs on any system with a JVM (Java Virtual Machine).

3. Simple & Easy to Learn
Java has a clean syntax, influenced by C/C++ but with many complexities removed (e.g., no pointers, no memory management by developer).

4. Secure
No direct memory access (no pointers).

Runs inside a sandbox, with built-in security features.     //// A sandbox in Java is a safe, restricted area where untrusted code runs with limited access to system resources like files or the internet.

Supports secure communication using cryptography, SSL, etc.

5. Robust
Strong memory management (via Garbage Collector).

Handles errors using exception handling.

Type checking at compile-time.

6. Multithreaded
Supports concurrent execution of two or more threads.

Built-in support via Thread, Runnable, ExecutorService, etc.

7. High Performance
Bytecode runs faster than interpreted languages.

JVM uses Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler to optimize performance.

8. Distributed
Java has libraries (like RMI, Socket, HTTP APIs) to build networked and distributed applications.

Also used in cloud and microservices via Spring Boot.

9. Dynamic
Java programs can load classes at runtime using reflection or class loaders.

Easily integrate libraries and modules during runtime.

10. Portable
Java code can run on any device or OS that has a JVM.

Data types and environment are fixed across platforms.

11. Architecture-Neutral
Java bytecode is not tied to a specific processor or OS.

This ensures cross-platform compatibility.

12. Rich Standard Library (API)
Java offers a large standard library including packages for:

Collections (java.util.*)

Networking (java.net.*)

I/O (java.io.*, java.nio.*)

Concurrency, Streams, Lambda, etc.

